# Who is asked to review a change.
#
# A single-maintainer project does not need path-level routing, but it does need
# the file to exist: without one, a pull request is assigned to nobody, and on a
# repository whose release path is a pushed tag the maintainer has no signal
# that something needs looking at (D9).
#
# Every path is claimed, deliberately.  A CODEOWNERS file that names only some
# directories reads as "the rest is unowned".

* @tkittich

# The release path is the one place where a mistake is public and permanent --
# a pushed tag is the entire release, and a mistyped version publishes a
# mislabelled artifact.  Listed separately so the intent is on the record even
# though the owner is the same.
/.github/workflows/ @tkittich
/.github/release-notes/ @tkittich
/pyproject.toml @tkittich
